WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:01.943
- [Mark] All right, Norman.

00:00:01.943 --> 00:00:02.910
- Yes, sir.

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:03.743
- [Mark] Welcome back.

00:00:03.743 --> 00:00:04.995
- Glad to be back.

00:00:04.995 --> 00:00:05.828
- [Mark] So what's the latest with you?

00:00:05.828 --> 00:00:09.030
- Well, the latest is, for
those who wanted to know,

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.700
did I nail the interview that Monday?

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.380
Yeah, I kicked its ass.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.483
I'm currently working for this company.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:16.450
We're not getting paid yet.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.540
I'm in the training process

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.780
because after I finished
the training process,

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.820
we'll be tested and I'll be
getting what you call a CPM,

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:26.340
which is a certified property
management certificate.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.080
And that's pretty good.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.573
You know, I'm working,
it's a 35-unit building.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.563
They housed veterans with severe PTSD.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.870
85% of them are ex-addicts

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.540
or using addicts now because
they have harm reduction

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:46.560
that's put in place.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.890
So that within itself is a blessing.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:55.100
You know, how do I get to a
point to where God blesses me

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:00.100
to move away from that in order
to move me into a position

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:05.080
and a situation where
people are just like me

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.606
and may need a helping hand.

00:01:08.606 --> 00:01:09.457
- [Mark] Who better than you?

00:01:09.457 --> 00:01:12.393
- You know, I mean, you
talk about grateful,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.610
I'm grateful that God has bestowed upon me

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.650
to even have a job.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.963
This place gave me a brand
new laptop that I work on.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.223
I haven't sold it.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:30.080
They trusted me, they're entrusting me.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.823
And the blessing about that
is that nobody trust me.

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:36.363
I didn't even trust myself.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:40.453
And there are some times
where I don't trust myself.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.360
But God is there.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.880
Situation being the other day,

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.163
I was coming home and the
police were chasing the guy,

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:51.940
and he dropped his dope sack.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:54.502
And I'd seen it.

00:01:54.502 --> 00:01:56.630
Now immediately, the
addict mind kicked in.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.900
Norman, look, you ain't got no money.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:00.080
Times are tough.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:03.210
You sober, you can take
this, you can sell this.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:04.357
And it just went on and on for a minute.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.457
And I had, all I said was God, be with me.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.330
I walked past it.

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:10.676
And when I turned around,

00:02:10.676 --> 00:02:12.480
another car was coming around the corner,

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.313
they opened the door

00:02:13.313 --> 00:02:15.203
and they went right straight to that sack.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:21.050
See, just because I'm
sober and I'm not using,

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:23.550
doesn't mean that the
addict mind doesn't kick in.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.120
It kicked in.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.800
But most importantly, I
did something about it.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.920
The best thing I could do about it: pray.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.190
Because usually I wouldn't
believe in prayer.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:36.143
Remember, God and I had a problem.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.440
Now we don't.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.360
I called on him.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.303
He helped me and walked me through it.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:45.240
That was very important for me,

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.890
because if I would have took that

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.580
and those police came around
that corner, I'm gone.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:52.990
I wouldn't be talking to you right now.

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:54.263
So thank God for that.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:00.000
The job is, how would I put this?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.880
It's nourishing for me.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.240
You know, because it's an older building

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:09.790
that was restored and it's 35 units.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.430
It's pretty small, but it's really nice.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:14.430
But I'm able to help some people.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:15.960
I'm able to be of service.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:20.960
You know, if you don't know
low income tax credits,

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.030
HUD housing, and things like that,

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.280
it'd be a very difficult job.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.740
Luckily, God has blessed me to work

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.990
for companies in the
past doing this stuff,

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.090
which led me to a position

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.080
where I know exactly what I'm doing.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.060
They've given me five tests already.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.683
I scored 100% on all five.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.290
It's not bragging.

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:40.920
It's not trying to toot my own horn.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:45.333
But thank God I got the ability
to even go through a test.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:48.300
'Cause I know that I have the aptitude

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.730
and the ability to do it.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.920
But what about those times
where I just said no.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:56.720
Sometimes I think about those times.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.610
It's Christmas time,

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:00.950
and of course, I miss my mom.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.100
I miss my grandmother.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.533
I miss my family in
general, but it's okay.

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:07.050
It's a little hard right now,

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.850
because they cut the food stamp thing off.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:09.890
I'm not getting paid from the job

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:12.040
but I'm still working, but it's okay.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.690
And know why it's okay?

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:16.680
Because God dammit exactly
what it's supposed to be.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.960
See, and I respect it more

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.800
because I remember those
times where I disrespected it

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:23.630
and didn't care.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:27.140
See, usually I'd be running
around acting a fucking fool,

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:27.973
but I'm not.

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:31.200
It's not that I'm
self-centered or self-seeking.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.200
I'm just into doing the
best that I can right now,

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:37.750
one day at a time.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.580
Because futuristically when I look further

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.503
than I'm supposed to, I fuck up.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:49.460
So God is allowing me
to learn from my past.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:53.210
I don't have to hold
on to it, like I have.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:57.400
I don't have to use it
as an excuse, as I have.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.910
But I can learn from it.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:00.743
Because I remember those times.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.900
I still have a place
to stay with my buddy.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:06.470
We have a little food.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:09.035
We're gonna get some
more, somehow some way.

00:05:09.035 --> 00:05:09.880
- [Mark] You're in a tent still?

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:10.713
- [Norman] Huh?

00:05:10.713 --> 00:05:11.546
- [Mark] You're in a tent?

00:05:11.546 --> 00:05:13.494
- No, I'm in Donald's,
I'm still at Donald.

00:05:13.494 --> 00:05:15.143
- [Mark] Oh wait so, you have a little...

00:05:15.143 --> 00:05:17.143
- Yeah, we got the
refrigerator we got, yeah.

00:05:17.143 --> 00:05:22.143
We don't have a lot, but I
thank God for the minimal.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.400
And the other day I was thinking,

00:05:27.253 --> 00:05:29.080
because for two days I was thinking about

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:30.130
thank God for the minimum.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:31.100
Thank God for the minimum.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.300
Thank God for the minimum.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.330
And so when I went into my
meditation the other morning,

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:37.310
I sat. because I go in a
Little Tokyo in Los Angeles,

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:40.460
and I sit by this pond that
has these goldfish, you know,

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.260
and they're very therapeutic for me.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:44.910
And I kept thinking, I was like,

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:48.214
why do you want me to to appreciate,

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:50.003
to be grateful for the minimum.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:54.023
And what came to me was so
you'll appreciate the maximum.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.880
So if I'm grateful for the minimum,

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.590
I'll more so appreciate
the maximum when it comes.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:02.450
I won't be selfish and self-centered,

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:05.760
I'll be conscious enough
to know that, guess what,

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.853
I moved from here to here.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.540
And I did it with God's help.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:13.880
Not about me, It's not all about me.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.030
You know, my friend is struggling

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:21.030
and he's really struggling, man.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:23.380
And it hurts

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.873
because I live with him.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:33.170
And to watch somebody just,
man, just tear themselves down.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.600
I try.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.370
I try my best,

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.780
but as God has instituted
in me to do one thing,

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:44.763
and one thing only, be my shining light.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.250
Norman, it's gonna happen when it happens.

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:50.580
Of course it hurts me,

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:53.050
'cause that's my friend, you know.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.560
Out of everybody, even
when I was down and out,

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.500
he let me in his house.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:58.740
I didn't have any fucking food.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:00.960
He had a minimal, very
minimal amount of food.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.670
He gave me something to eat.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.640
He allowed me to wash my ass.

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:06.563
He let me sleep on his floor.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.490
Still he's doing this.

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.827
So I'm gonna pray for him.

00:07:12.827 --> 00:07:14.710
I'm not gonna excuse myself for crying

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.200
because sometimes some people say,

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.300
well man's not supposed to cry.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.670
Well, what the fuck I have tear ducts for?

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.290
Why do I have emotions?

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.740
You know, I love that brother
'cause he's a good brother.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.550
And all I want, you know,
is the best for him.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.756
So it'll happen when it happens there.

00:07:28.756 --> 00:07:29.589
- [Mark] Yeah, just because you want it

00:07:29.589 --> 00:07:30.680
doesn't mean he's ready.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.350
- Yeah, it has to come in his time.

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:33.183
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:07:33.183 --> 00:07:35.990
- So the other day I ran
into a good friend of mine

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:37.410
who went through elementary school with me

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:39.620
from kindergarten to sixth grade.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:43.700
And he was really struggling,
but he knew who I was.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:45.973
Now, you're talking 40 plus years ago.

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:49.020
And I asked him, I said,
"Hey man, how you doing?"

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:52.150
And he says, "Man, this
crystal meth and this crack.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.347
It's tearing me apart."

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:57.070
He said, "My marriage is gone,

00:07:57.070 --> 00:08:00.157
and everybody just doesn't
wanna be bothered with me."

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:04.277
And I asked him, I said,
"Why do you do it?"

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:06.870
He said,

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:09.487
"Because I really just don't
wanna deal with anything."

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.570
I said, "Well, just do me a favor."

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:16.550
I said, "Take my number
down and call me, anytime."

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:17.760
I said, "I want you to know this."

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.080
I said, "I don't know how long I have."

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:22.020
I said, "But I've been
clean for a little minute."

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:22.853
Just a little minute.

00:08:22.853 --> 00:08:25.170
I don't know how long because
I don't count the days.

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:27.600
I said, "Just believe in God

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:29.500
and ask him to take it away from you."

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:31.687
And he said, "Okay."

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:36.423
His mom called me this morning.

00:08:37.578 --> 00:08:38.411
- [Mark] Good.

00:08:38.411 --> 00:08:41.950
And that woman said, you know,
"I just wanna thank you."

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:44.090
She said, "I don't remember you."

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:46.463
His mother is 90 plus years old.

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:50.080
She said, "I don't remember you.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:53.340
But he told me you guys
went to school together."

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.577
She said, "Whatever you
said to my son, thank you."

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.320
And I said, "Well, you know."

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:01.090
She says, "No, honey.

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:05.130
Whatever you said to that
boy, it touched him."

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:08.507
She said, "Iban has not
touched anything in four days."

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:11.860
And, you know, I'm a
very emotional guy, man.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:13.370
You know, I cry like a baby,

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.270
like I got tears in my eyes now.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:18.160
Because, you know,
coming from me, come on,

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.910
you know the crack head
Norman, one check Norman,

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:23.800
smoke up everything Norman.

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:26.160
How the fuck do you put me in the position

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:28.420
to where I wasn't
looking at doing anything

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.550
but just saying a kind word.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:32.030
And his mom called me

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:36.060
and she said a prayer
for me on that phone.

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:38.140
My buddy wasn't there.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:39.303
I cried like a baby.

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:44.270
And I just thank God for putting
me in a position like this,

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.840
to be his shining light

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:47.803
and to do his bidding and not my own.

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.283
I just wanna help people,

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:54.530
which in turn helps me, you know.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:56.320
Even the negative comments.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.610
Some people say, well you
haven't done anything.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:09:59.443
Well, guess what?

00:09:59.443 --> 00:10:01.060
That's your opinion.

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:04.200
As long as I feel within myself
that I've done something,

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.350
and I have all these positive comments,

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:09.420
the positive always outweighs
the negative, you know.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:12.210
So I'm gonna keep on keeping on.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:14.360
I'm gonna keep on doing
exactly what I'm doing

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:16.580
in order to get where I need to go.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:19.150
I don't know where I need to go.

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:21.630
I know where I would want to go,

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:23.843
but God knows exactly where I'm going.

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:26.070
So I'll just ride that train.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:29.370
And with that, everybody
have a good holiday.

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:31.650
You know, eat enough, don't get sick.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:34.290
Thank you very much for your prayers

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:37.490
and your just being you.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:38.670
Thank you so very much.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:39.503
- [Mark] Excellent, Norman.

00:10:39.503 --> 00:10:40.540
Thank you very much, man.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:41.480
You look great.

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:42.313
- Thank you.

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:44.890
That shit broke my fucking heart, man.

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:48.970
That lady and she was crying
and I'm like, oh my God.

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:51.360
She said "Whatever you said to him."

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.920
Yeah, he's been clean for four days.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:55.540
- [Friend] He remembered
me from fucking...

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.818
We were in class from
kindergarten to 6th grade!

00:10:58.818 --> 00:10:59.651
- [Mark] But isn't it great

00:10:59.651 --> 00:11:00.580
to be able to help somebody like that?

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:02.126
- [friend] Yeah!

00:11:02.126 --> 00:11:04.793
(voices fading)

